# CoreText format 1 retains circular history instead of destructively popping.
# Apple's written rules specify destructive pops and clearing on Reset:
# https://developer.apple.com/fonts/TrueType-Reference-Manual/RM06/Chap6kerx.html
# Native CoreText instead retains eight circular slots, initially pointing to
# the first glyph of the run. Each action list walks backwards from the latest
# push and wraps every eight values; zero values also advance that cursor.
# The Reset flag is ignored. Legacy kern retains its existing pop rules.
# These 35 cases were measured on macOS 15.8.2 and 26.6.2.
# stack-leftover
